<< /Alt (The organisation of content diagram consists of a central circle showing the Working Scientifically skills: Questioning and Predicting, Planning Investigations, Conducting Investigations, Processing Data and Information, Analysing Data and Information, Problem Solving, and Communicating. The central circle is surrounded by a ring divided in into the Year 11 and Year 12 modules. The Year 11 modules are: Module 1 Properties and Structure of Matter, Module 2 Introduction to Quantitative Chemistry, Module 3 Reactive Chemistry and Module 4 Drivers of Reactions. The Year 12 modules are: Module 5 Equilibrium and Acid Reactions, Module 6 Acid/Base Reactions, Module 7 Organic Chemistry and Module 8 Applying Chemical Ideas.) /K [ 9 ] /P 153 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
